# Documentation guardrails (Design System)

## Content integrity

- **Never invent** system-specific facts, component behavior, token semantics, dimensions, or color values. Every stated value must come from Figma, token JSON, or an explicit design decision.
- If information is missing or unverified, write `TBD` and add an item under **Gaps / TBD**.
- No code examples for now (design-only documentation).
- Do not leave editorial placeholders such as `TODO`, `XXX`, `{placeholder}`, or `<placeholder>` in committed docs.

## Structure and consistency

- Use stable headings and the same section order for pages of the same type. See `component-doc.mdc` for component pages.
- Component pages must use only the canonical allowed H2 headings from `component-doc.mdc` (no extra H2 sections).
- Apply canonical `component_name` normalization and deterministic path rules from `component-name-normalization.mdc`.
- Every component doc should start with a one-line description immediately after the H1.
- Component pages should include `### Visual Proof` inside `## Overview` (not as a new H2). This subsection stores screenshot evidence and related metadata.
- Prefer tables for properties, states, and token mappings. Use consistent column order across all tables of the same kind.
- Apply page taxonomy from `docs-taxonomy.mdc` (`component`, `overview`, `workflow`) and keep scope boundaries clear.
- `## Gaps / TBD` follows a deterministic contract:
  - present only when unresolved gaps exist,
  - omitted when no gaps exist,
  - items must use checkbox format `- [ ] [GAP_TYPE] ...`.

## Pipeline order and preconditions

- Follow the canonical stage contract in `docs-pipeline-contract.mdc`.
- Source of truth: the component spec. Markdown and Figma sections are derived artifacts.

## Token references

- Token names must match the JSON keys exactly and be wrapped in inline code (e.g., `` `Semantic.Color.Focus-Outline.Inner` ``).
- Always pair a token path with its resolved hex fallback — either in parentheses or in a dedicated table column.
- See `token-references.mdc` for naming conventions and formatting rules.

## Figma references

- Reference Figma by **component set name** and **property name** only.
- Follow `prohibited-patterns.mdc`.
- Figma node IDs are allowed in source links and metadata (for example, `node-id` in source URLs or explicit node references in metadata).
- Do not use node IDs as token identifiers; keep token references human-readable.
- For deterministic markdown -> Figma placement, prefer `figma.component_set_node_id` from the spec.
- For visual evidence capture, use the screenshot workflow:

```bash
npm run ds:capture-visual-proof -- --component-name <ComponentName> --agent codex
```

- Store proof metadata in `docs/_generated/visual-proofs/` and link it from `### Visual Proof` under `## Overview`.

## Metadata

- Component docs must carry a lifecycle status consistent with `markdown-lifecycle-status.mdc`.
- Component specs must declare `status`: `draft` or `ready`.
- Component specs in `ready` status must include a concrete `figma.component_set_node_id`.
- Generated files in `docs/_generated/` must not be hand-edited; they are overwritten by skills.

## Editorial consistency

- Follow language and tone rules from `docs-language-tone.mdc`.
- For component docs, include Figma metadata from `component-figma-metadata.mdc`.
- Keep overview/index pages synchronized per `overview-index-maintenance.mdc`.
- Ensure internal markdown links resolve to real local targets.
